  <HaltConditions>
    | 🛑 ID | Trigger |
    |---|---|
    | `H_NO_INPUT` | Neither findings / bug nor a code change to reconcile |
    | `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE` | Cannot tell fix from from-code — ask the operator |
    | `H_OPERATOR_REJECT` | Operator rejected the reconcile plan |
    | `H_TRIVIALITY_UNCONFIRMED` | Fix looks trivial but the probe leaves doubt, OR no critic was dispatched (a self-probe does not confirm triviality) — ask the operator: short-circuit or full path |
    | `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL` | Gates still fail after the reconcile |
  </HaltConditions>

  <ExecutionPlan>
    <Step id="STEP_0_INTAKE">
      <Goal>Detect the mode.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Findings / bug / review present → `fix`. Code already changed / "formalize what I coded" / drift
        → `from-code` (`AX_MODE_AUTO_DETECT_OR_HALT`; ambiguous → `H_AMBIGUOUS_MODE`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_0B_PREFLIGHT">
      <Goal>Clear the FLOW_VERSION/READINESS preflight gate before mapping the affected area.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Use the `FLOW_VERSION` / `READINESS` fields from the `sdd-state` snapshot already produced by
        the skill's GATHER step; do not call `sdd-state` or `sdd-task` again here. Size the gate to this
        request's own blast radius (`AX_PREFLIGHT_BLAST_RADIUS_SCOPED`): v1 intersecting legacy task
        layout → `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/migration-v1-v2.directive.xml")`;
        not-ready and this reconcile needs a missing gate →
        `READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/readiness.directive.xml")`;
        otherwise record the out-of-scope state in one line and continue.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_1_PICTURE">
      <Goal>Map the affected area. (mechanical → tools)</Goal>
      <Action>
        Intent-search the specs for the area in play + read the git diff; map which specs / tasks own it
        (`orient` for the entity / contract surface, `sdd-check` for the link / tracker state). This
        is the bounded read — not the whole repo.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2_PROBE">
      <Goal>Probe the spec against the problem — the critical step (`AX_PROBLEM_PROBES_SPEC`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Dispatch the critic on the affected spec, seeded with the problem, to judge: **bug or spec-defect**
        (code violates a right spec, or the spec was wrong); **the class** (where
        else the same class occurs, via `orient` over the closed-world); **the blast radius** (what
        else the diff touches). MUST cover the full problem class and blast radius — the reported symptom is only the entry point. The critic MUST be an actually dispatched subagent — an
        orchestrator self-probe never satisfies this step and never confirms triviality, no matter how
        small the fix looks (mirrors `AX_FIX_CLASSIFICATION`: triviality is confirmed by the probe, never
        by self-assessment). No dispatched verdict → `H_TRIVIALITY_UNCONFIRMED`. The probe verdict feeds STEP_2B.
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_2B_CLASSIFY">
      <Goal>Resolve ownership, classify every finding — BEFORE any edit (`AX_FIX_CLASSIFICATION`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        Build the ownership map first (`AX_TASK_RESOLUTION`): per finding located in a `.ts` / `.spec.md`
        file — read the file header (first lines before `import` / first `#`), extract
        `@tasks: <ACR>-<slug>[, ...]`, build file → [Task-IDs]. Header absent → classify anyway (the fix
        IS adding the header), note "no task" for the plan.

        Classify each finding into an action category:
        - **direct-fix** — global / non-code artifact: tracker desync, execution-log placeholder, a
          missing header with no other findings. Edit the file directly, verify.
        - **spec-update** — spec gap: missing inventory entity, DbC contract gap, Decision Log gap,
          stale pivot artifact. Edit the spec; a spec change that invalidates code escalates to task-reopen.
        - **task-reopen** — ANY finding in a code file carrying `@tasks:`: bug, contract violation,
          missing test, BDD mismatch, review finding. Reopen the owning task per `AX_REOPEN_FORMAT`;
          pair every code-fix phase with a `test` phase (regression); multiple findings of one task go
          into a single reopen Round.

        <LogicSwitch on="fix class — confirmed by the dispatched critic's verdict from STEP_2, never by self-assessment (self-probe is void)">
        - WHEN the class is trivial: a single site, blast radius confirmed empty by the dispatched critic's verdict, contracts / specs untouched -> patch the code TOGETHER WITH a regression test covering the fixed case in the same run (a task-reopen always pairs code-fix with a `test` phase — the trivial branch is not exempt from that pairing just because it skips the Round), back-sync the spec (`sdd-sync`), then run the gate: `npx gennady sdd-verify --profile code` — the SAME ladder every phase runs, never a hand-assembled "typecheck + the touched tests" substitute. The trivial branch skips the Round, not the verification: a self-picked command set is exactly how an unverified change reaches DONE, and on a stub project it would prove nothing at all (the ladder refuses those, this branch would not).
          - WHEN the gate is green -> present `FIX_SUMMARY_FORMAT`. DONE — the full tail (STEP_3–7, audit + code-review over the reconciled set) stays skipped.
          - WHEN the gate prints a line carrying BOTH the `⛔` marker AND the words `обязательная ступень профиля` (verification infrastructure missing or stubbed — the gate name sits between them, and `⛔` alone also opens the ordinary halt line for a plain compile/test failure, which is fixable here as usual) -> NOT fixable from here and NOT a reason to fall back to a lighter check: surface it to the operator naming the missing scripts, and stop. The trivial path has no verified outcome on such a project.
          - WHEN the gate is red AND the failure reproduces on the pre-change baseline AND lies outside the blast radius confirmed by the critic -> record it in `FIX_SUMMARY_FORMAT` as pre-existing (not caused by this patch), propose a separate task to the operator for it, and do NOT head the summary with "✅ complete" — the gate is still red. DONE.
          - OTHERWISE (the failure is caused by or overlaps the patch/blast radius) -> `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL`.
        - WHEN triviality is plausible but the probe leaves doubt -> `H_TRIVIALITY_UNCONFIRMED`
        - DEFAULT -> STEP_3_PLAN, the full path
        </LogicSwitch>
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_3_PLAN">
      <Goal>Plan what moves.</Goal>
      <Action>
        From the probe + STEP_2B categories, decide per item what moves: code → spec (fix the code via
        execution) or spec → code (`AX_PIVOT_REQUIRES_SUPERSESSION` + cascade downstream) or both;
        reopen / create the affected tasks (`AX_REOPEN_FORMAT`), including the class siblings; group
        scattered edits sharing one intent into a single task (`AX_GROUPING_REDUCES_NOISE`) — per-finding
        tasks are noise; reconcile any new entity via `orient` (`AX_REUSE_FIRST`), filling the
        "Reuse rationale" slot for anything that lands on JUSTIFY. If STEP_2B found a file with a
        missing header, the plan MUST carry an explicit line to add it — the fix IS adding the header;
        this is not deferred to `sdd-sync`, which does not write headers. Present the plan
        (`PLAN_TABLE_FORMAT`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_4_AGREE">
      <Goal>Operator agreement (`AX_OPERATOR_AGREEMENT`).</Goal>
      <Action>Ask via `QUESTION_RULE_SLIM`; warn about the class / blast the operator may not have seen (`AX_OPERATOR_SAFEGUARD`). Rejected → `H_OPERATOR_REJECT`. STOP.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_5_APPLY">
      <Goal>Apply the changes.</Goal>
      <Action>
        Apply spec edits (defect / from-code); reopen / create tasks per the STEP_2B ownership map
        (`AX_TASK_RESOLUTION`); dispatch the reopened tasks through execute as a BATCH with per-task
        audit skipped (`AX_DISPATCH_VIA_BATCH`; the dispatched workers stay spec-bound per
        `AX_SPEC_IS_SOLE_SOURCE`) — one reconcile-level verify runs at STEP_7 instead
        (`AX_EXECUTION_ORDER`, `AX_HANDOFF_TYPED`, route per `AX_FINDING_ROUTING`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_6_SYNC">
      <Goal>Back-sync — mandatory in BOTH modes.</Goal>
      <Action>`sdd-sync` brings specs / tasks / trackers into agreement with the final code. This tail is the same whether we entered as fix or from-code.</Action>
    </Step>
    <Step id="STEP_7_VERIFY">
      <Goal>Verify mechanically AND semantically (`AX_VERIFY_AT_END`).</Goal>
      <Action>
        This full tail applies to the DEFAULT (non-trivial) path only — the trivial fix class already
        exited at STEP_2B, where it ran the SAME phase gate every phase runs, `sdd-verify --profile
        code` (never a hand-assembled "typecheck + touched tests" substitute). Reaching STEP_7 means
        the path is non-trivial: run this full tail once here, never as an extra "to be safe" pass
        layered on top of an already-closed trivial path.

        `sdd-check` must pass — a fast mechanical integrity pass over the reconciled specs/tickets
        (else `H_VERIFICATION_FAIL`). Do NOT run `sdd-verify --profile full` here. Because the
        group-audit hook was skipped in the batch (`AX_DISPATCH_VIA_BATCH`), restore the safety net
        ONCE at the reconcile level by dispatching a fresh-eyes audit
        (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/audit.directive.xml")`, scoped to every spec + ticket
        touched by the reconciliation — drift code↔spec over that reconciled set, not the formal
        `AX_AUDIT_MODES` per-group cycle). That audit's OWN STEP_1 is the SINGLE owner of the full
        mechanical gate (`sdd-verify --profile full` + `gennady lint --spec` + `testcov`) over the
        reconciled set — running `full` here too would pay for the whole ladder twice. Also dispatch a
        code-review (`READ_AND_USE_DIRECTIVE("ai/directives/sdd-v2/code-review.directive.xml")` — bugs in the
        reconciled diff). A `BLOCKER` from either MUST pause and surface to the operator. Present the
        reconcile summary (`FIX_SUMMARY_FORMAT`).
      </Action>
    </Step>
  </ExecutionPlan>

